---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { HRPAUTH, PROFILE, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="I'm Samuel Cheston, the independent developer behind MatchCore, HRPAuth, Cascade, and Silo40. Here's the idea that started the work."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main id="main" class="shell about-main">
			<a class="text-link back-link" href="/"><span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span> Back to the work</a>
			<div class="about-heading">
				<p class="eyebrow">About / Samuel Cheston</p>
				<h1>One developer.<br /><span class="accent-text">The whole picture.</span></h1>
				<p class="hero-description">I build across the stack because the things I want to make don't stop at one layer.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="about-grid">
				<aside class="about-facts" aria-label="At a glance">
					<dl>
						<div><dt>Who</dt><dd>Samuel Cheston</dd></div>
						<div><dt>How I work</dt><dd>Independent developer</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Main focus</dt><dd>MatchCore ecosystem</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Currently</dt><dd>Rapid iteration on HRPAuth</dd></div>
					</dl>
					<a class="text-link" href={PROFILE.github}>GitHub profile <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
				</aside>
				<div class="about-story">
					<section aria-labelledby="starting-point">
						<p class="eyebrow">The starting point</p>
						<h2 id="starting-point">It began with matchmaking.</h2>
						<p>
							MatchCore started with an idea: bring ELO-MMR matchmaking to Minecraft.
							That remains the original goal behind an ecosystem that now includes
							authentication, web interfaces, and tools that connect to the game.
						</p>
						<p>
							I independently develop these projects, from the underlying services
							to the interfaces around them. HRPAuth is one part of that larger effort,
							not the whole story.
						</p>
					</section>
					<section aria-labelledby="foundation">
						<p class="eyebrow">An engineering choice</p>
						<h2 id="foundation">Build the foundation you need.</h2>
						<p>
							There was already a mature option for Minecraft authentication and skins:
							Blessing Skin. For my plans, though, I felt its technology choices constrained
							how far I could take the system.
						</p>
						<p>
							I chose to build a new foundation. HRPAuth is my approach to authentication
							and skin management within MatchCore, with a Go backend and a dedicated
							web frontend. It has {HRPAUTH.users} real users and is still evolving rapidly.
						</p>
						<a class="text-link" href={HRPAUTH.url}>Read the HRPAuth source <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
					</section>
					<section aria-labelledby="beyond">
						<p class="eyebrow">Other parts of the work</p>
						<h2 id="beyond">From network protocols to game systems.</h2>
						<p>
							Cascade explores the infrastructure side: a Rusted Warfare edge proxy,
							routing players to independent backends and integrating HRPAuth authentication.
						</p>
						<p>
							Silo40 explores a different kind of system: a strategy game set in the world
							of Wool, with survival, ideology, and multiple paths for civilization.
							I independently develop both projects.
						</p>
					</section>
					<section aria-labelledby="now">
						<p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
						<h2 id="now">Still building MatchCore.</h2>
						<p>
							My focus is still on these projects, especially the ongoing iteration
							of HRPAuth and the ecosystem around it.
						</p>
						<div class="about-actions">
							<a class="button button-dark" href={PROFILE.ecosystem}>Explore MatchCore <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
							<a class="text-link" href="/#connect">Connect <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
						</div>
					</section>
				</div>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
